WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:127826

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.602
We now have two A2A servers,

2
00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:05.572
an insurance policy agent and a health research agent.

3
00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:07.974
Let's have them work on a task together.

4
00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:10.377
You'll use a sequential agent from ADK,

5
00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:12.879
which will handle the A2A communications

6
00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:14.881
and call the two agents in sequence,

7
00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:17.784
feeding the results from one agent into the next using

8
00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:20.020
A2A clients. Let's dive in.

9
00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:23.823
Now we're going to create a sequential workflow chain agent with ADK

10
00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:26.626
using the previous agents we've already created.

11
00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:28.194
First, I'll make sure that both

12
00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:30.030
of the previous agents are still running.

13
00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.632
You can see in terminal one,

14
00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:35.335
I have the insurance policy agent still running.

15
00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:38.772
Now, let's open terminal 2.

16
00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:40.673
And I can see that the

17
00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:42.308
health research agent is also still running.

18
00:00:42.609 --> 00:00:44.911
If not, be sure to run the uv run

19
00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:47.247
command again as you did in the previous lessons.

20
00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.749
You can find the instructions in your notebook.

21
00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.252
Then, I'll import the libraries,

22
00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:56.256
including the RemoteA2Aagent class from ADK.

23
00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.558
and the SequentialAgent class.

24
00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:00.827
and InMemoryRunner.

25
00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:03.296
And I'll disable warnings as before.

26
00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:05.598
Then I'll load in the environment variables.

27
00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:08.802
Note, this time, I need to pull in the host

28
00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:12.605
and the ports for both the policy agent and research agent.

29
00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:14.808
Now, to connect to the A2A agents,

30
00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:18.611
you just need to instantiate the class RemoteA2Aagent,

31
00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:20.313
give the agent a name,

32
00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:22.015
and pass in the URL for

33
00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:23.850
where the agent card will be hosted.

34
00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.853
I'll do this for both the policy_agent

35
00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.956
and the health_research_agent.

36
00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:32.659
This RemoteA2Aagent class

37
00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:34.727
acts as your A2A client.

38
00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:37.230
and it handles all of the boilerplate code

39
00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.932
for interacting with an A2A agent,

40
00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:41.034
like the HTTP connections,

41
00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:42.735
tasks, and messages.

42
00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:46.206
Next, I'll create an ADK SequentialAgent,

43
00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:48.708
which will have the health_research_agent,

44
00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:51.411
and policy_agent as sub_agents.

45
00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:54.614
Note, because this is a SequentialAgent,

46
00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:58.384
the order of these agents listed under sub_agents does matter.

47
00:01:58.685 --> 00:02:00.887
It determines which agent is called first.

48
00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:03.990
This is different if you're using an LLMAgent,

49
00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:06.693
which has the model decide which agent to call when.

50
00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:10.697
Now, I can send a single request to the sequential agent

51
00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:13.700
and it should give me a response from both agents.

52
00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:17.070
I'll create an InMemoryRunner to store the agent state.

53
00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.439
and then run it with the prompt.

54
00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:22.442
and print out the final response.

55
00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:26.946
And here we can see responses from the health research agent,

56
00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:33.653
and our policy agent, tailored to our specific insurance policy.

57
00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:36.689
And there you go. You've successfully

58
00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:39.659
built a chained multi-agent system using A2A.

59
00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:42.462
Next up, we'll build yet another agent

60
00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:45.165
using A2A and MCP.
